+BLOCKED: A-103 unmet — the no-JS flow T-103's contract mandates is broken by a
+Content-Type gap in the merged feature. `GET /probe` never sets a Content-Type
+(`internal/web/probe.go` probeGet writes the fragment bare), Go's response
+sniffing does not classify `<h2>`-leading content as HTML (unlike pages, whose
+`<!DOCTYPE html>` prefix IS a sniff signature), so the fragment is served as
+`text/plain; charset=utf-8` — and the global `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
+(`internal/web/web.go:94`) makes every browser honor that literally. A no-JS
+visitor following the contract's `<a href="/probe">Probe</a>` link sees inert
+markup text: no heading, no readable count, no submittable form, so the
+`303 -> /` flow is unreachable without JS. HTMX is unaffected (it swaps
+responseText as HTML), which is why every JS-on test passes and only the
+no-JS e2e runs are red. Fix: one line in `internal/web/probe.go` (set
+`Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8` before writing the fragment, in
+probeGet and the HTMX POST path) — a file no task currently owns; planner
+action requested (cut a fix task owning `internal/web/probe.go`). After it
+lands, this branch's `make check` is green with ZERO further test edits.
+
