+  probe section (server-rendered or plain form)") is looser than the draft
+  test encoded from it. The draft's no-JS clause asserted a superseded
+  mechanism — a draft-side defect, so I edited the TEST to the operative
+  contract (rule 3, second bullet; edit #3 below).
+- Following the operative contract's link exposed the REAL feature gap: the
+  fragment page is served `text/plain` (diagnosis in the BLOCKED header,
